  "conclusions": [
    "Default Vulkan vision encoding reproduces fence expiration and severely incorrect finite embeddings even when the text decoder uses CPU. A successful HTTP response is insufficient for correctness.",
    "CPU vision plus GPU text produces the expected layout prefix. Serialized GPU vision plus CPU text produces the same prefix, with cosine similarity 0.999926 to CPU embeddings.",
    "Serial submissions complete the real advanced OCR page with 19 blocks and no kernel GPU error. This is a validated workaround for this device and software stack, not a proof of universal Intel GPU stability.",
    "Evidence isolates asynchronous large-image Vulkan vision execution interacting with i915/Mesa. Exact responsibility between llama.cpp synchronization, Mesa/ANV, and i915 scheduling/watchdog is not fully bisected.",
    "The recorded 20-second kernel request watchdog is consistent with the observed fence expiration; it is separate from application inference timeouts.",
    "This reproducer runs ONNX on CPU and does not exercise WebGPU NHWC; it cannot establish a common root cause with the older ONNX issue."
  ],
  "recommendations": [
    "Short term: set GGML_VK_SERIALIZE_SUBMISSIONS=1 before starting a fresh process on this Linux Intel iGPU; retain existing device selection.",
    "If automating the workaround, initially target the actually selected Linux Intel integrated PCI 8086:7d51 device; do not apply it to unrelated AMD/NVIDIA discrete GPUs.",
    "Alternative CLI path: --no-mmproj-offload with GPU text generation; verified only on the 32-token minimal layout prefix, not a full advanced page.",
    "Upstream PR30438 addresses a different GPU-to-host barrier issue on Intel/Mesa and remains unmerged as checked; it has not been validated for this timeout and is not asserted to fix it."
  ],
